/target
# cargo-fuzz build output. `fuzz/corpus/` and `fuzz/artifacts/` are tracked on
# purpose: the corpus is the curated seed set and the artifacts are crash
# regressions that `tests/fuzz_corpus.rs` replays on every run.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/coverage
# Where a fuzz run accumulates what it discovers. libFuzzer writes new units to
# the first corpus directory it is given, so runs are pointed here and
# `fuzz/corpus/` stays exactly the seed set the replay gate polices — a
# discovered input is kept for reaching new coverage, which is not the same
# property the gate's work floor checks.
/fuzz/corpus-run
/artifacts
/tmp
package-lock.json
package.json
node_modules
# .claude is tracked so shared config (skills, hooks, settings.json) is available to all contributors.
# Files matching *.local.* are personal and not shared — keep them out of source control.
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/*.local.*
.idea
.local-utils
.worktrees.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
